          "title": "You'll want to know: രക്ഷകൻ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "രക്ഷകൻ — rakṣakan — \"a rescuer; a saviour\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ ചെറുപ്പക്കാരൻ ഗ്രാമത്തിന്റെ രക്ഷകനായി. ā ceṟuppakkāran grāmattinṟe rakṣakanāyi. That young man became the village's saviour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun രക്ഷ means protection; a woman rescuer is രക്ഷക."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "രക്ഷകൻ (rakṣakan) is borrowed from Sanskrit rakṣaka, \"protecting, guarding\" (Monier-Williams), with the Malayalam masculine ending -ൻ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
